---
import ContentLayout from '~/layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import AgentDiagram from '~/components/AgentDiagram.astro';
import DecisionTool from '~/components/DecisionTool.astro';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Foundations"
  description="How deterministic routing and agentic extraction operate across the post-market safety pipeline."
  eyebrow="01 — Foundations"
  heading="The architecture of modern pharmacovigilance."
  lede="True automation in drug safety relies on two vastly different technological primitives. One rigidly routes structured E2B XML payloads; the other reads unstructured clinical literature and reasons like a medical reviewer. Knowing exactly when to deploy which is the foundation of a defensible safety system."
>

  <!-- ─── THE TWO ENGINES ─── -->
  <section class="engines-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="engines-grid">

        <!-- Workflow -->
        <article class="engine wf">
          <span class="engine-tag wf-tag">Deterministic Workflow</span>
          <h2>The E2B compliance router</h2>
          <p class="engine-deck">
            Rule-based integration layers designed to enforce rigorous, predictable logic across structured databases and safety systems.
          </p>
          <ul class="traits">
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-8" stroke="#16A684" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
              <span><strong>E2B (R3) transmission.</strong> Flawlessly generates, validates, and transmits AS2 gateway submissions to the FDA, EMA, and PMDA.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-8" stroke="#16A684" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
              <span><strong>Immutable audit trails.</strong> Every action is mathematically verifiable, making it perfect for CIOMS I form generation and 21 CFR Part 11 compliance.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M8 1v14M1 8h14" stroke="#C06A24" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              </svg>
              <span><strong>Brittle to ambiguity.</strong> If a field is missing, or a patient email contains unstructured jargon, the deterministic engine halts and flags a human.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class="engine-foot">
            Deployed when the data is structured, the rules are rigid, and the regulatory penalty for deviation is severe.
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Agentic -->
        <article class="engine ag">
          <span class="engine-tag ag-tag">Agentic AI</span>
          <h2>The semantic extractor</h2>
          <p class="engine-deck">
            Large Language Models configured as autonomous agents capable of interpreting complex clinical narratives and extracting structured events.
          </p>
          <ul class="traits">
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-8" stroke="#E08A2B" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
              <span><strong>Contextual MedDRA coding.</strong> Maps complex verbatim terms to the correct Lowest Level Term (LLT) by reasoning through the surrounding clinical context.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-8" stroke="#E08A2B" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
              <span><strong>Unstructured intake.</strong> Digests 30-page PDF hospital discharge summaries and separates relevant adverse events from background medical history.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-8" stroke="#E08A2B" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
              <span><strong>Causality synthesis.</strong> Drafts structured safety narratives by correlating concomitant medications, dechallenge results, and patient demographics.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class="engine-foot ag-foot">
            Deployed when raw inputs are unstructured (literature, emails, calls) and require expert clinical judgement to categorise.
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="relation">
        These systems do not compete. The modern safety architecture deploys <strong>agentic extraction for the unstructured intake</strong>, which then feeds cleanly structured XML into <strong>deterministic workflow systems for regulatory routing</strong>.
      </p>

      <!-- ── Volume vs Headcount Chart ── -->
      <div class="cmp-table-wrap" id="metrics">
        <h2 class="cmp-table-title">The Breaking Point: ICSR Volume vs Manual PV Headcount</h2>
        <div class="chart-container">
          <div class="y-axis">
            <span>200%</span>
            <span>150%</span>
            <span>100%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chart-area">
            <!-- ICSR Volume Curve -->
            <svg class="chart-line-volume" viewBox="0 0 800 200" preserveAspectRatio="none">
              <path d="M0,180 C200,170 400,120 800,20" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-amber-bright)" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
            </svg>
            <div class="chart-label label-volume">ICSR Volume Growth (+15-20% YoY)</div>
            
            <!-- PV Headcount Curve -->
            <svg class="chart-line-headcount" viewBox="0 0 800 200" preserveAspectRatio="none">
              <path d="M0,180 C200,185 400,175 800,170" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-green-bright)" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray="8 8" />
            </svg>
            <div class="chart-label label-headcount">PV Headcount (Flat Budgets)</div>
          </div>
          <div class="x-axis">
            <span>2020</span>
            <span>2022</span>
            <span>2024</span>
            <span>2026</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="chart-caption">
          The traditional model of throwing more medical reviewers at the problem has mathematically failed. Agentic automation is the only viable mechanism to decouple safety processing capacity from headcount.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── AGENT ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM ─── -->
  <section class="diagram-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <AgentDiagram />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── PHARMA AI ORCHESTRATOR ─── -->
  <section class="orchestrator-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="orch-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Agentic Case Processing</span>
        <h2>The Pharmacovigilance AI Orchestrator: <em>clinical logic at scale</em></h2>
        <p class="orch-lede">
          In production, agentic AI operates via multi-agent orchestration. A single "triage" agent receives unstructured intake (e.g., a rambling email from a patient), decomposes it into specialised clinical subtasks, and dispatches them to domain-specific agents—such as a MedDRA coder or seriousness evaluator. The results are synthesized into a coherent, E2B-ready output for human review.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Cinematic PV Image -->
      <div class="cinematic-image-wrapper">
        <img src="/images/pv_orchestrator.png" alt="A cinematic rendering of AI in a pharmaceutical laboratory, glowing green and amber neural nodes" class="cinematic-img">
      </div>

      <div class="orch-callouts">
        <div class="oc-item">
          <span class="oc-num">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Valid Case Detection</h3>
            <p>The orchestrator ingests noisy inputs and immediately tests against the four minimum criteria for a valid ICSR: identifiable patient, identifiable reporter, suspect drug, and adverse event.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="oc-item">
          <span class="oc-num">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Specialist Agent Dispatch</h3>
            <p>Subtasks route to specialists. A coding agent evaluates PT/LLT mappings. A temporal agent calculates the time-to-onset from drug exposure. A literature agent cross-references PubMed for similar signals.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="oc-item">
          <span class="oc-num">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Human-in-the-Loop Review</h3>
            <p>Before regulatory submission, the orchestrator surfaces the drafted E2B fields to a QPPV (Qualified Person Responsible for Pharmacovigilance) with full reasoning traces and highlighted source texts.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── WHY PHARMA ─── -->
  <section class="why-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">02 — The Intake Crisis</span>
        <h2>A highly regulated function <em>drowning in unstructured data.</em></h2>
        <p>Few domains combine such enormous unstructured case volume, heavy clinical documentation, and unforgiving regulatory deadlines. Agentic automation was built precisely to absorb this unstructured friction.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Cinematic Unstructured Data Image -->
      <div class="cinematic-image-wrapper">
        <img src="/images/pv_unstructured_data.png" alt="Unstructured medical documents dissolving into a structured stream of glowing green and amber data" class="cinematic-img" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      </div>

      <div class="why-grid">
        <div class="why-card">
          <svg class="why-ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6">
            <path d="M12 2v20M2 12h20" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/>
          </svg>
          <h3>Global Reporting Explosion</h3>
          <p>Global adverse event reporting is growing exponentially due to stricter pharmacovigilance legislation (e.g., GVP Module VI) and easier patient reporting portals.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <svg class="why-ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6">
            <rect x="4" y="3" width="16" height="18" rx="2"/>
            <path d="M8 8h8M8 12h8M8 16h5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
          <h3>Unstructured Clinical Intake</h3>
          <p>Safety data rarely arrives cleanly. It requires reading through complex, rambling unstructured PDFs, physician notes, and noisy social media monitoring feeds.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <svg class="why-ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6">
            <path d="M12 3l8 4v5c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V7l8-4z" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          <h3>Strict Expedited Deadlines</h3>
          <p>Global agency rules—like the strict 15-day expedited reporting window for SUSARs—demand incredibly fast, traceable, and consistent medical assessment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <svg class="why-ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6">
            <circle cx="12" cy="8" r="4"/>
            <path d="M4 20c0-4 3.5-6 8-6s8 2 8 6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
          <h3>Expensive Medical Review</h3>
          <p>Highly trained Medical Doctors spend 60% of their time on copy-pasting administrative data entry rather than performing complex causality and signal detection.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <svg class="why-ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6">
            <path d="M4 4h16v16H4zM8 4v16M4 12h4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
          <h3>The Deduplication Bottleneck</h3>
          <p>The same adverse event is often reported by a patient, a physician, and a pharmacist simultaneously. Identifying exact duplicates across databases is a manual nightmare.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <svg class="why-ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6">
            <path d="M5 12h14M5 12l4-4M5 12l4 4M19 7v10" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          <h3>Disconnected Safety Systems</h3>
          <p>Siloed databases (Argus, ArisG, Veeva Vault) make signal detection slow. Transporting data between them relies heavily on brittle integrations and human bridges.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── Next pages CTA ─── -->
  <section class="next-section">
    <div class="wrap next-inner">
      <a href="/safety-pipeline" class="btn btn-primary magnetic">See the safety pipeline →</a>
      <a href="/case-studies" class="btn btn-ghost magnetic">See it in practice</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</ContentLayout>

<script>
  // Intersection Observer for chart lines
  const chartObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach((entry) => {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) {
        entry.target.classList.add('animate-draw');
      }
    });
  }, { threshold: 0.5 });

  document.querySelectorAll('.chart-line-volume path, .chart-line-headcount path').forEach((el) => {
    chartObserver.observe(el);
  });
</script>

<style>
  /* ── Engines ── */
  .engines-section {
    padding: 5rem 0;
    background-color: #13201b;
    color: #f1ece0;
  }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .engines-section {
    background-color: #14211d;
  }
  .engines-section .eyebrow { display: none; } 

  .engines-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .engine {
    border: 1px solid rgba(241,236,224,.18);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 2.4rem 2.1rem;
    transition: transform 280ms ease, border-color 280ms ease;
  }
  .engine:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    border-color: rgba(241,236,224,.38);
  }

  .engine-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 5px 11px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .wf-tag { background: var(--color-green-bright); color: #0d1614; }
  .ag-tag { background: var(--color-amber-bright); color: #0d1614; }

  .engine h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0.4rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: #f1ece0;
  }
  .engine-deck {
    color: rgba(241,236,224,.72);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .traits {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }
  .traits li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: rgba(241,236,224,.88);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .traits li svg { flex: none; margin-top: 3px; }
  .traits li strong { color: #f1ece0; font-weight: 600; }

  .engine-foot {
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(241,236,224,.14);
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: rgba(241,236,224,.62);
  }

  .relation {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: rgba(241,236,224,.8);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    max-width: 48em;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .relation strong {
    color: var(--color-amber-bright);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ── Cinematic Images ── */
  .cinematic-image-wrapper {
    margin: 3rem auto;
    max-width: 1000px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(241, 236, 224, 0.1);
    box-shadow: 0 30px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  }
  .cinematic-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 21 / 9;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 40%;
    display: block;
    transition: transform 0.8s ease;
  }
  .cinematic-image-wrapper:hover .cinematic-img {
    transform: scale(1.02);
  }

  /* ── Custom Data Chart ── */
  .cmp-table-wrap {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    background-color: rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
    border: 1px solid rgba(241,236,224,.1);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .cmp-table-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-green-bright);
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(241,236,224,.1);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .chart-container {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr;
    grid-template-rows: 250px 30px;
    padding: 2rem 3rem 1rem 1rem;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .y-axis {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: rgba(241,236,224,.5);
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .x-axis {
    grid-column: 2;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: rgba(241,236,224,.5);
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    border-top: 1px dashed rgba(241,236,224,.2);
  }
  .chart-area {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }
  .chart-line-volume, .chart-line-headcount {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    overflow: visible;
  }
  /* Animation for drawing the paths */
  .chart-line-volume path, .chart-line-headcount path {
    stroke-dasharray: 1000;
    stroke-dashoffset: 1000;
  }
  .chart-line-volume path.animate-draw {
    animation: drawLine 2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) forwards;
  }
  .chart-line-headcount path.animate-draw {
    animation: drawLine 2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) forwards;
    animation-delay: 0.3s;
    stroke-dasharray: 8 8 1000; /* Preserve dash pattern while animating */
  }
  @keyframes drawLine {
    to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
  }
  .chart-label {
    position: absolute;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.8);
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
  }
  .label-volume {
    top: 5px;
    right: 0;
    color: var(--color-amber-bright);
    transform: translateY(-50%);
  }
  .label-headcount {
    bottom: 30px;
    right: 0;
    color: var(--color-green-bright);
  }
  .chart-caption {
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
    padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: rgba(241,236,224,.8);
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-align: center;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(241,236,224,.1);
  }

  /* ── Diagram section ── */
  .diagram-section {
    padding: 4rem 0;
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  /* ── Orchestrator section ── */
  .orchestrator-section {
    padding: 5rem 0;
    background-color: #0a1510;
  }
  .orch-head { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .orch-head .eyebrow { color: var(--color-green-bright); margin-bottom: 0.7rem; display: block; }
  .orch-head h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.8rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #f1ece0;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .orch-head h2 em { color: var(--color-green-bright); font-style: italic; }
  .orch-lede {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: rgba(241,236,224,.68);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 62em;
  }
  
  .orch-callouts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .oc-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    background: rgba(241,236,224,.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(241,236,224,.1);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }
  .oc-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-green-bright);
    flex: none;
    padding-top: 3px;
  }
  .oc-item h3 {
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #f1ece0;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .oc-item p {
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: rgba(241,236,224,.6);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Why Pharma ── */
  .why-section {
    padding: 5.5rem 0;
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
  }
  .sec-head {
    max-width: 52em;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  .sec-head h2 { margin-top: 0.9rem; font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.8vw, 3rem); }
  .sec-head p { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--color-text-2); line-height: 1.6; }

  .why-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
  }
  .why-card {
    padding: 2.1rem 1.9rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-line-soft);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line-soft);
    transition: background-color 200ms ease;
  }
  .why-card:hover { background-color: var(--color-surface-2); }
  .why-card:nth-child(3n) { border-right: 0; }
  .why-card:nth-child(n+4) { border-bottom: 0; }
  .why-ic {
    width: 38px;
    height: 38px;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }
  .why-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.28rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .why-card p { font-size: 0.93rem; color: var(--color-text-soft); line-height: 1.55; }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .engines-grid, .why-grid, .orch-callouts {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .why-card { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line-soft); }
    .chart-container {
      padding: 1rem;
      grid-template-columns: 40px 1fr;
    }
    .label-volume, .label-headcount {
      position: relative;
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 1rem;
      top: auto; right: auto; bottom: auto; transform: none;
    }
  }
</style>
